{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210691,"nonce":"u7YChydsrDFUUaCPN1x73fhxHDY=","title":"Diagnostics: error squiggle and stack trace wrong once a function has tiered up","message":"Commit 6720026 fixed span reporting for the bytecode-only path. Once any function in the error chain has been tier-up'd the squiggle lands on the wrong line (often a comment) and the trace shows getter-style methods (viewProj, data, ...) sandwiched between user frames.\n\nRoot cause: JIT and threaded frames deposit nothing into mir_frames, so unwinding has no func_id + pc for native frames. Fix needs a stack-trace shim per native frame (or a parallel structure keyed by return address, which the GC stack walker already resolves via code_range lookups).\n\nReliable signal that this is the case: a trace with getter names between user code, or a squiggle on a comment line.","files":null}]}